{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A confirmed merge can be reported as needing review or landing when the saved PR snapshot is stale or missing."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The digest invites review during an active changes round, when a submitted review will be refused."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An external push can invalidate an acknowledged approval without causing the digest to surface the PR for another review."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A previously blocked land remains visible after a confirmed external merge and can prompt unnecessary investigation."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A large unread candidate backlog causes repeated serial requests at session start, although material latency was not measured."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"diag","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Invisible and bidirectional characters can affect visual presentation, but the reproduction shows no escape from the quoted data boundary."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"An exceptionally long question is inserted in full into every session digest and can consume substantial agent context."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An incomplete or older PR observation can cause status to present an obsolete failed review round instead of the unknown current head."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"normal","reason":"Each applicable detail request performs an extra indexed lookup without a demonstrated incorrect result or material performance impact."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"MCP review approvals are persistently attributed to a human, making the recorded provenance inaccurate without changing authorization."},{"id":"C12","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Codex following the documented consumer name can miss unread activity after Claude advances the shared cursor."}]}